.TH OFTC 1 "October 14, 2026" "OFTC 1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
oftc \- standalone macOS FortiGate IPsec VPN client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oftc setup
.br
.B oftc setup
\fB\-\-import\fR \fINAME\fR
.br
.B oftc setup
\fB\-\-gateway\fR \fIHOST\fR \fB\-\-saml\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR [\fB\-\-tcp\fR]
.br
.B oftc setup
\fB\-\-from\-development\fR
.br
.B oftc connect
.br
.B oftc disconnect
.br
.B oftc status
.br
.B oftc uninstall
[\fB\-\-erase\-profile\fR]
.br
.B oftc help
.SH DESCRIPTION
OFTC uses the signed macOS app to own the VPN configuration, Keychain PSK,
system extension, SAML sign-in, and supervised reconnection.
The package installs the app and this command at their standard paths.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup
Prepare a profile, activate OFTC's system extension, and add its macOS VPN
configuration. It does not connect. With no options and no existing profile,
ask which local settings to use. The OFTC development profile and FortiClient
profiles, when present, provide editable gateway and SAML port defaults. A
matching FortiClient credential is tried before asking for a PSK in the
terminal. With an existing OFTC profile, resume setup.
.TP
.BI "setup \-\-import " NAME
Import a local FortiClient profile and its PSK. Existing OFTC profiles are not
overwritten. If the saved PSK is unavailable, use interactive
.B setup
to keep its connection settings and enter the PSK at the terminal prompt.
.TP
.BI "setup \-\-gateway " "HOST \-\-saml\-port PORT"
Save a new OFTC profile and prompt for its PSK in the terminal. UDP is the
default outer transport. Add
.B \-\-tcp
to select TCP.
.TP
.B setup \-\-from\-development
Copy the nonsecret OFTC development profile and prompt for its PSK under the
release app's Keychain identity if no matching saved FortiClient PSK is
available. This is only for migration from the OFTC
development build. Stop the old VPN and its login agent first.
.TP
.B connect
Start a supervised VPN connection. The per-user login agent is installed if
needed and enabled for future GUI logins. A browser sign-in may be required.
Recoverable connection failures are retried by the supervisor.
.TP
.B disconnect
Stop the VPN and disable automatic login starts. A deliberate disconnect stays
down until the next
.BR "oftc connect" .
.TP
.B status
Show VPN state, nonsecret profile settings, login agent state, and CHILD SA
rekey counts while connected.
.TP
.B uninstall
Disconnect OFTC, remove its per-user login agent and VPN configuration,
deactivate its system extension, and invoke the package removal helper with
administrator access. Profile, Keychain PSK, and logs are retained by default.
The helper refuses to remove the app while the extension remains active.
.TP
.B uninstall \-\-erase\-profile
Also erase the OFTC profile and its exact Keychain PSK after disconnecting.
.TP
.B help
Show a short command summary.
.SH DEVELOPMENT OPTION
.TP
.BI "\-\-app " /absolute/path/OFTC.app
Prefix
.BR setup ,
.BR connect ,
or
.B status
to target a development build. The login agent records that app path.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /Applications/OFTC.app
Installed app and system extension.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/oftc
Command-line tool.
.TP
.I ~/Library/Logs/OFTC/agent.log
Per-user supervised connection log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B systemextensionsctl(8)
